## Safety and durable state

Keep the Fireworks key only in `~/.openclaw/.env` with mode 0600. Do not print credentials, place them in a command argument, commit them, or copy them into a Codex prompt. Use provider environment resolution. Process inventories must show only PIDs, parents, status, and executable names (for example `ps -p <pid> -o pid=,ppid=,stat=,comm=`); never print full process arguments or environments with `pgrep -fl`, `ps ... args`, or similar, since other apps can embed credentials there. Keep the Gateway bound to loopback; the existing private Tailscale Serve endpoint provides desktop/mobile access. Before destructive cleanup, verify targets and retain a recoverable reference. Keep `state/` and `logs/` private. Only the transient heartbeat launcher returns `NO_REPLY` after successful dispatch; the visible heartbeat conversation always leaves a readable result.
